    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Lead sheet",
      "body": "A **lead sheet** is a song written as the tune with chord symbols above it. The singer reads the tune, and the band reads the symbols and plays each chord until the next one appears.\n\n**Why it matters:** It is the standard way bands share songs. Read the symbols and you can play along with any song on a lead sheet.",
